# Every .env variant, however it got made. .env and .env.bak* were listed but
# an editor's own backup is not named either -- nano writes .env.save, and that
# file holds the same database credentials, JWT secrets and payment keys as the
# original. One `git add -A` on the server is all it takes.
.env.*
!.env.example
